AudD  ·  profile default
                 │ Help › Keys
 1 Recognize     │  Getting started  Guide  Commands >Keys< Exit codes  Links 
 2 Now playing   │ Moving around
 3 Streams       │   Menu on the left, page on the right. Arrows move, Enter goes in, Esc comes back.
 4 Recognitions  │   The menu is the sidebar; Help, Streams, Recognitions, and Account have a tab bar above their page.
 5 Account       │   On a choice ‹ like this ›, ←/→ change it and ← on its first option goes back. When a text field is
 6 Settings      │   selected, you are typing in it: letters, digits, and symbols go in, ←/→ move the cursor (← at its
*7 Help          >   start goes back), ctrl+u clears it, and esc stops typing but keeps the value and the form (enter
                 │   types again; then 1-7 jump to a section). Recognize opens typing in its File, URL, or folder field;
                 │   other pages open with no text field selected. After an error the cursor is back in the field it is
                 │   about. A saved value, such as the callback URL, is changed only after enter or e, and esc puts the
                 │   old value back. Enter in a form's last text field runs it (in Add a stream, enter in ID adds it;
                 │   the box below is optional). What a page can do is on its buttons: tab (or ↓ from the end of the
                 │   page) reaches them, ←/→ move between them, enter presses one. A letter on a button, such as (o),
                 │   presses it from anywhere on the page. A key works only where it is listed; any other key says it
                 │   does nothing. Settings of audd and a stream's URL save right away; u or ctrl+z undoes the last
                 │   change until you make another or leave the section. Spending requests, removing, signing out, or
                 │   replacing the token asks in a dialog: every dialog opens on Cancel; ←/→ or tab move to the action
                 │   and enter presses it (or click it); n or esc cancels. y copies the command at the bottom
                 │   everywhere, in a dialog too.
                 │ 
                 │   ↑/↓            move in the menu, a list, or a form
                 │   → or enter     go in: open the section, the page, the selected item
                 │   ← or esc       come back one level (in typed text ← moves the cursor)
                 │   ←/→            on a tab bar: switch tabs; on a choice: change it
                 │   ↑              from the top of a page: back to its tab bar
                 │   [ ]            previous or next tab, from anywhere in the section outside text fields
                 │ 
                 │ Everywhere
                 │   1-7            jump to a section (not while typing in a text field)
                 │   ctrl+k or :    run any command; ctrl+k again closes it
                 │   y              copy the command shown at the bottom (in a dialog too)
                 │   ?              keys for this screen
                 │   F1             help
 [ Commands ]    │   q              quit; it asks first when something typed is not saved or a command runs (not while
